course: dictionary
lesson: 11206
title: One woman, many women
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: A woman is a grown-up female person, an adult girl. «A young woman» is a woman who is not very old yet, and «an old woman» is one who has lived for a long time. The word tells you the person is grown up, not a child.
explain: When there is more than one, the word changes. Women is the word for more than one woman. Say «one woman» and «two women». Do not write «two womans», because the word is women.
explain: Look at the words around it to check the meaning. «The policewoman waved the bus on» tells you that policewoman is a job done by a woman. Words like businesswoman and policewoman join woman to another word, so the whole word tells you who the person is.
fact: A woman is a grown-up female person.
fact: Women is the word for more than one woman.
fact: Women is spelled with an e at the end of the first part: woman, women.
fact: «Businesswoman» and «policewoman» are made from woman and another word.
fact: «England's women's football team, the Lionesses,» won the European Championship in 2022 and again in 2025.
exercise: What is a woman? | A small child | A man with a beard | A kind of boat | *A grown-up female person
exercise: What is the word for more than one woman? | womans | womens | woman | *women
exercise: In «The women and men walked to the park», which word is the plural of woman? | park | walked | *women | man
test: Which sentence uses the word correctly? | Three womens came in. | Three woman came in. | *Three women came in. | Three womans came in.
test: Which word means a woman who is a police officer? | womanhood | policeman | *policewoman | businessman
exam: Complete the sentence: «Two ___ ran the race.» | woman | womans | womens | *women
